{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ד'", :translit "dalet", :gloss "[the Name, by way of abbreviation]"} {:he "הביאני", :translit "hevi'ani", :gloss "He brought me"} {:he "במסודה בצדקתי הביאני ה'", :translit "b'mesudah b'tzidkati hevi'ani Hashem", :gloss "into His pavilion, in righteousness He brought me, YHWH"} {:he "במראות אלהים הביאני אל ארץ ישראל", :translit "b'mar'ot Elokim hevi'ani el eretz Yisra'el", :gloss "in visions of Elohim He brought me to the land of Israel"} {:he "הביאני אל בית היין", :translit "hevi'ani el beit ha-yayin", :gloss "He brought me into the house of wine"} {:he "הביאני המלך חדריו", :translit "hevi'ani ha-melech chadrov", :gloss "He brought me, the King, into His chambers"} {:he "שראתה שפחה על הים מה שלא ראה יחזקאל", :translit "she-ra'ata shifchah al ha-yam mah she-lo ra'ah Yechezkel", :gloss "that a maidservant at the sea saw what Ezekiel did not see"} {:he "במראות אלהים הביאני", :translit "b'mar'ot Elokim hevi'ani", :gloss "in visions of Elohim He brought me"} {:he "שכלם היו נביאים וזכו למראה", :translit "she-kulam hayu nevi'im ve-zachu li-m'rah", :gloss "that all of them were prophets and merited vision"} {:he "במתן תורה", :translit "b'matan Torah", :gloss "at the giving of the Torah"} {:he "הביאני אל בית היין", :translit "hevi'ani el beit ha-yayin", :gloss "He brought me into the house of wine"} {:he "לפני הר סיני", :translit "lifnei Har Sinai", :gloss "before Mount Sinai"} {:he "ונתן לי התורה שנדרשת בשבעים פנים", :translit "ve-natan li ha-Torah she-nidreshet b'shiv'im panim", :gloss "and gave me the Torah, which is expounded in seventy faces"} {:he "הביאני חדריו", :translit "hevi'ani chadrov", :gloss "He brought me into His chambers"} {:he "והראני השמים ושמי השמים", :translit "ve-hir'ani ha-shamayim u-shmey ha-shamayim", :gloss "and showed me the heavens and the heaven of heavens"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Collects four scriptural occurrences of the phrase 'הביאני' and reads them as a progressive sequence of revelation."} {:kind :other, :note "Identifies Song of Songs verses as alluding to historical events: Sinai, the splitting of the sea, and the revelation of the celestial realms."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'a maidservant at the sea saw what Ezekiel did not see' originates in the Mekhilta's exposition on the Song at the Sea (Exodus 15:1). Ezekiel's visions are recorded in Ezekiel 1, yet the tradition states that even the lowest-ranking Israelite at the sea surpassed that prophetic level. The Torah being 'expounded in seventy faces' corresponds to the tradition that the Torah was given in seventy languages (Shabbat 88a) or that it has seventy facets (Numbers Rabbah 13:15). The phrase 'showed me the heavens and the heaven of heavens' echoes Deuteronomy 10:14. The four-fold repetition of 'He brought me' (Song of Songs 2:4, 2:4 [variant reading of 'הביאני'], 1:4, and 1:4) is read by the Midrash as alluding to four moments of divine bringing: into the pavilion of the sea, into the land of Israel in prophetic vision, to Sinai for the Torah, and into the celestial chambers (Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:4, 1:12; 2:4).", :sources ["Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Shirata, ch. 1" "Shabbat 88a" "Numbers Rabbah 13:15" "Deuteronomy 10:14" "Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:4" "Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:12" "Shir HaShirim Rabbah 2:4" "Ezekiel 1" "Exodus 15:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Collects four scriptural occurrences of the phrase 'הביאני' and reads them as a progressive sequence of revelation.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Identifies Song of Songs verses as alluding to historical events: Sinai, the splitting of the sea, and the revelation of the celestial realms.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:35.629121874Z", :model "glm-5.2"}